cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below, and also cite the HPO and Phenopacket Store papers listed under references."
title: "HPO-PTBR Lab: mapping Brazilian Portuguese phenotype terms to the Human Phenotype Ontology"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Rondinelle
    family-names: Walitte
    alias: "Rondinelle Walitte Pedro de Jesus"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-1776-2754"
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/rondinellewalitte/fenotipo-br"
abstract: >-
  Research pilot measuring how well Brazilian Portuguese phenotype terms map to the Human
  Phenotype Ontology (HPO) when only English labels are searched, and how much of published
  rare-disease case descriptions already has an official Portuguese HPO label. Research
  support only; not a clinical or diagnostic tool.
keywords:
  - Human Phenotype Ontology
  - Brazilian Portuguese
  - rare diseases
  - phenotype normalization
  - sentence embeddings
  - phenopackets
references:
